ysis.", "newValue": "The Confederation of North, Central America and Caribbean Association Football (CONCACAF), founded on September 18, 1961, in Mexico City, is a pivotal governing body in international soccer, overseeing competitions involving 41 member associations across North America, Central America, and the Caribbean. As a cornerstone of the global football community, its establishment marked a significant moment in the organization of the sport, influencing how football was played and governed in its regions and contributing to a growing sense of unity and identity among member nations.

